{"task_id": "Mbpp/100", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the next smallest palindrome of a specified integer, returned as an integer.\nassert next_smallest_palindrome(99)==101\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef next_smallest_palindrome(n):\n    # Convert to string and find the next palindrome\n    s = str(n + 1)\n    \n    while True:\n        if s == s[::-1]:\n            return int(s)\n        \n        # Try to make current number a palindrome by mirroring left half\n        length = len(s)\n        mid = length // 2\n        \n        if length % 2 == 0:\n            # Even length\n            left_half = s[:mid]\n            candidate = left_half + left_half[::-1]\n        else:\n            # Odd length\n            left_half = s[:mid]\n            middle_char = s[mid]\n            candidate = left_half + middle_char + left_half[::-1]\n        \n        if int(candidate) > int(s):\n            return int(candidate)\n        \n        # Need to increment the middle part\n        if length % 2 == 0:\n            # Even length - increment right-most digit of left half\n            left_num = int(s[:mid]) + 1\n            left_str = str(left_num).zfill(mid)\n            if len(left_str) > mid:\n                # Overflow, need more digits\n                s = '1' + '0' * (length - 1) + '1'\n                return int(s)\n            candidate = left_str + left_str[::-1]\n        else:\n            # Odd length - increment middle digit first, then left half if needed\n            middle_digit = int(s[mid])\n            if middle_digit < 9:\n                left_half = s[:mid]\n                new_middle = str(middle_digit + 1)\n                candidate = left_half + new_middle + left_half[::-1]\n            else:\n                # Middle digit is 9, need to increment left half\n                if mid == 0:\n                    # Single digit 9\n                    return 11\n                left_num = int(s[:mid]) + 1\n                left_str = str(left_num).zfill(mid)\n                if len(left_str) > mid:\n                    # Overflow\n                    s = '1' + '0' * (length - 1) + '1'\n                    return int(s)\n                candidate = left_str + '0' + left_str[::-1]\n        \n        return int(candidate)\n```"}
