{"task_id": "Mbpp/119", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the element that appears only once in a sorted array.\nassert search([1,1,2,2,3]) == 3\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef search(arr):\n    \"\"\"Find the element that appears only once in a sorted array using binary search.\"\"\"\n    left, right = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    \n    while left < right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        \n        # If mid is odd, make it even by decrementing\n        if mid % 2 == 1:\n            mid -= 1\n            \n        # If pair is intact, unique element is on the right\n        if arr[mid] == arr[mid + 1]:\n            left = mid + 2\n        else:\n            right = mid\n            \n    return arr[left]\n```"}
