{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes in positive integers m and n and finds the number of possible sequences of length n, such that each element is a positive integer and is greater than or equal to twice the previous element but less than or equal to m.\nassert get_total_number_of_sequences(10, 4) == 4\n\"\"\"\ndef get_total_number_of_sequences(m, n):\n    \"\"\"Count sequences where each element >= 2*previous and <= m.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    if n == 1:\n        return m\n    \n    # dp[i][j] = number of sequences of length i ending with value j\n    dp = {}\n    \n    # Base case: sequences of length 1\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        dp[(1, j)] = 1\n    \n    # Fill for lengths 2 to n\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, m + 1):\n            dp[(i, j)] = 0\n            # Previous element must be <= j//2 to satisfy j >= 2*prev\n            for prev in range(1, min(j // 2, m) + 1):\n                dp[(i, j)] += dp.get((i - 1, prev), 0)\n    \n    # Sum all sequences of length n\n    total = 0\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        total += dp.get((n, j), 0)\n    \n    return total"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the next perfect square greater than a given number.\nassert next_Perfect_Square(35) == 36\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef next_Perfect_Square(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the next perfect square greater than n.\"\"\"\n    import math\n    sqrt_n = int(math.sqrt(n))\n    if sqrt_n * sqrt_n == n:\n        return (sqrt_n + 1) ** 2\n    else:\n        return (sqrt_n + 1) ** 2\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes in positive integers m and n and finds the number of possible sequences of length n, such that each element is a positive integer and is greater than or equal to twice the previous element but less than or equal to m.\nassert get_total_number_of_sequences(10, 4) == 4\n\"\"\"\ndef get_total_number_of_sequences(m, n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the number of valid sequences of length n where each element is >= 2*previous and <= m.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    if n == 1:\n        return m\n    \n    # dp[i][j] = number of sequences of length i ending with value j\n    dp = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    # Base case: sequences of length 1\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        dp[1][j] = 1\n    \n    # Fill the dp table\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, m + 1):\n            # For ending with value j, previous value must be <= j//2\n            for prev in range(1, min(j // 2, m) + 1):\n                dp[i][j] += dp[i-1][prev]\n    \n    # Sum all sequences of length n\n    return sum(dp[n])"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes an array and finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array, where a sequence is bitonic if it is first increasing and then decreasing.\nassert max_sum([1, 15, 51, 45, 33, 100, 12, 18, 9]) == 194\n\"\"\"\ndef max_sum(arr):\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n    \n    # Calculate increasing subsequence sums ending at each index\n    inc = [0] * n\n    inc[0] = arr[0]\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        inc[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                inc[i] = max(inc[i], inc[j] + arr[i])\n    \n    # Calculate decreasing subsequence sums starting at each index\n    dec = [0] * n\n    dec[n-1] = arr[n-1]\n    for i in range(n-2, -1, -1):\n        dec[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                dec[i] = max(dec[i], arr[i] + dec[j])\n    \n    # Find maximum bitonic sum\n    max_bitonic = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        max_bitonic = max(max_bitonic, inc[i] + dec[i] - arr[i])\n    \n    return max_bitonic"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to convert complex numbers to polar coordinates.\nassert convert(1) == (1.0, 0.0)\n\"\"\"\ndef convert(z):\n    \"\"\"Convert complex number to polar coordinates (magnitude, angle).\"\"\"\n    import math\n    if isinstance(z, (int, float)):\n        z = complex(z)\n    magnitude = abs(z)\n    angle = math.atan2(z.imag, z.real)\n    return (magnitude, angle)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\nassert lps(\"TENS FOR TENS\") == 5\n\"\"\"\ndef lps(s):\n    n = len(s)\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    \n    # Every single character is a palindrome of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n    \n    # Check for palindromes of length 2 and more\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                if length == 2:\n                    dp[i][j] = 2\n                else:\n                    dp[i][j] = dp[i + 1][j - 1] + 2\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n    \n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\nassert lps(\"TENS FOR TENS\") == 5\n\"\"\"\ndef lps(s):\n    \"\"\"Find length of longest palindromic subsequence using dynamic programming.\"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n    \n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                if length == 2:\n                    dp[i][j] = 2\n                else:\n                    dp[i][j] = dp[i + 1][j - 1] + 2\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n    \n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
