{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes an array and finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array, where a sequence is bitonic if it is first increasing and then decreasing.\nassert max_sum([1, 15, 51, 45, 33, 100, 12, 18, 9]) == 194\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef max_sum(arr):\n    \"\"\"Find maximum sum of bitonic subsequence (increasing then decreasing).\"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n    \n    n = len(arr)\n    \n    # Calculate LIS ending at each index\n    lis = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n):\n        lis[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                lis[i] = max(lis[i], lis[j] + arr[i])\n    \n    # Calculate LDS starting at each index\n    lds = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n-1, -1, -1):\n        lds[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                lds[i] = max(lds[i], lds[j] + arr[i])\n    \n    # Find maximum bitonic sum\n    max_bitonic = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        max_bitonic = max(max_bitonic, lis[i] + lds[i] - arr[i])\n    \n    return max_bitonic\n```"}
