{"task_id": "Mbpp/255", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes in a list and length n, and generates all combinations (with repetition) of the elements of the list and returns a list with a tuple for each combination.\nassert combinations_colors( [\"Red\",\"Green\",\"Blue\"],1)==[('Red',), ('Green',), ('Blue',)]\n\"\"\"\ndef combinations_colors(colors, n):\n    \"\"\"Generate all combinations with repetition of given length.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return [()]\n    \n    result = []\n    for color in colors:\n        for combo in combinations_colors(colors, n - 1):\n            result.append((color,) + combo)\n    \n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/255", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes in a list and length n, and generates all combinations (with repetition) of the elements of the list and returns a list with a tuple for each combination.\nassert combinations_colors( [\"Red\",\"Green\",\"Blue\"],1)==[('Red',), ('Green',), ('Blue',)]\n\"\"\"\ndef combinations_colors(colors, n):\n    \"\"\"Generate all combinations with repetition of length n from colors list.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return [()]\n    \n    result = []\n    \n    def generate_combinations(current_combination, remaining_length):\n        if remaining_length == 0:\n            result.append(tuple(current_combination))\n            return\n        \n        for color in colors:\n            current_combination.append(color)\n            generate_combinations(current_combination, remaining_length - 1)\n            current_combination.pop()\n    \n    generate_combinations([], n)\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function that takes in a non-negative number and returns the number of prime numbers less than the given non-negative number.\nassert count_Primes_nums(5) == 2\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef count_Primes_nums(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the count of prime numbers less than n.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Sieve of Eratosthenes\n    is_prime = [True] * n\n    is_prime[0] = is_prime[1] = False\n    \n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if is_prime[i]:\n            for j in range(i*i, n, i):\n                is_prime[j] = False\n    \n    return sum(is_prime)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function that takes in a non-negative number and returns the number of prime numbers less than the given non-negative number.\nassert count_Primes_nums(5) == 2\n\"\"\"\ndef count_Primes_nums(n):\n    \"\"\"Count prime numbers less than n using sieve of eratosthenes.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return 0\n    \n    is_prime = [True] * n\n    is_prime[0] = is_prime[1] = False\n    \n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if is_prime[i]:\n            for j in range(i*i, n, i):\n                is_prime[j] = False\n    \n    return sum(is_prime)"}
