{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function takes in an integer and check whether the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\nassert validate(1234) == True\n\"\"\"\ndef validate(num):\n    # Convert to string to access individual digits\n    num_str = str(abs(num))\n    \n    # Count frequency of each digit\n    digit_count = {}\n    for digit in num_str:\n        digit_count[digit] = digit_count.get(digit, 0) + 1\n    \n    # Check if frequency <= digit value for each digit\n    for digit, count in digit_count.items():\n        if count > int(digit):\n            return False\n    \n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the largest sum of a contiguous array in the modified array which is formed by repeating the given array k times.\nassert max_sub_array_sum_repeated([10, 20, -30, -1], 4, 3) == 30\n\"\"\"\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr, n, k):\n    # Handle edge cases\n    if not arr or k <= 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Create the repeated array\n    repeated_arr = arr * k\n    \n    # Apply Kadane's algorithm to find maximum subarray sum\n    max_sum = repeated_arr[0]\n    current_sum = repeated_arr[0]\n    \n    for i in range(1, len(repeated_arr)):\n        current_sum = max(repeated_arr[i], current_sum + repeated_arr[i])\n        max_sum = max(max_sum, current_sum)\n    \n    return max_sum"}
