{"task_id": "Mbpp/300", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the count of all binary sequences of length 2n such that sum of first n bits is same as sum of last n bits.\nassert math.isclose(count_binary_seq(1), 2.0, rel_tol=0.001)\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef count_binary_seq(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns count of binary sequences of length 2n where sum of first n bits equals sum of last n bits.\"\"\"\n    from math import comb\n    total = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        total += comb(n, k) * comb(n, k)\n    return total\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to calculate the maximum aggregate from the list of tuples.\nassert max_aggregate([('Juan Whelan',90),('Sabah Colley',88),('Peter Nichols',7),('Juan Whelan',122),('Sabah Colley',84)])==('Juan Whelan', 212)\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef max_aggregate(tuples_list):\n    # Calculate sum of values for each name\n    aggregates = {}\n    for name, value in tuples_list:\n        aggregates[name] = aggregates.get(name, 0) + value\n    \n    # Find the name with maximum aggregate value\n    max_name = max(aggregates, key=aggregates.get)\n    return (max_name, aggregates[max_name])\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/305", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to return two words from a list of words starting with letter 'p'.\nassert start_withp([\"Python PHP\", \"Java JavaScript\", \"c c++\"])==('Python', 'PHP')\n\"\"\"\ndef start_withp(word_list):\n    \"\"\"Returns the first two words starting with 'p' from the given list.\"\"\"\n    p_words = []\n    for item in word_list:\n        words = item.split()\n        for word in words:\n            if word.lower().startswith('p'):\n                p_words.append(word)\n                if len(p_words) == 2:\n                    return tuple(p_words)\n    return tuple(p_words)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/300", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the count of all binary sequences of length 2n such that sum of first n bits is same as sum of last n bits.\nassert math.isclose(count_binary_seq(1), 2.0, rel_tol=0.001)\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef count_binary_seq(n):\n    # Use combinatorial approach: C(2n, n) represents choosing n positions out of 2n for 1s\n    # When n 1s are placed in 2n positions, the constraint is automatically satisfied\n    def factorial(num):\n        if num <= 1:\n            return 1\n        result = 1\n        for i in range(2, num + 1):\n            result *= i\n        return result\n    \n    def combination(n, k):\n        if k > n or k < 0:\n            return 0\n        return factorial(n) // (factorial(k) * factorial(n - k))\n    \n    return float(combination(2 * n, n))\n```"}
