{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum sum of increasing subsequence from prefix until ith index and also including a given kth element which is after i, i.e., k > i .\nassert max_sum_increasing_subseq([1, 101, 2, 3, 100, 4, 5 ], 7, 4, 6) == 11\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, n, i, k):\n    # Find max sum of increasing subsequence from prefix until i, including element at k\n    max_sum_until_i = 0\n    dp = [0] * n\n    \n    # Calculate max sum increasing subsequence ending at each position up to i\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        dp[j] = arr[j]\n        for prev in range(j):\n            if arr[prev] < arr[j]:\n                dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[prev] + arr[j])\n        max_sum_until_i = max(max_sum_until_i, dp[j])\n    \n    # Find best subsequence ending at position <= i that can extend to k\n    best_sum = 0\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[j] < arr[k]:\n            best_sum = max(best_sum, dp[j])\n    \n    return best_sum + arr[k]\n```"}
