{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to set the left most unset bit.\nassert set_left_most_unset_bit(10) == 14\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n):\n    # Find the position of the leftmost unset bit and set it\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Create a mask to find the leftmost unset bit\n    temp = n\n    position = 0\n    \n    # Find the highest set bit position\n    while temp > 0:\n        temp >>= 1\n        position += 1\n    \n    # Check each bit from left to right to find first unset bit\n    for i in range(position, -1, -1):\n        if not (n & (1 << i)):\n            return n | (1 << i)\n    \n    # If all bits are set, set the next higher bit\n    return n | (1 << position)\n```"}
