{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum sum possible by using the given equation f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\nassert get_max_sum(60) == 106\n\"\"\"\ndef get_max_sum(n):\n    # Memoization to store computed results\n    memo = {}\n    \n    def helper(num):\n        if num in memo:\n            return memo[num]\n        \n        if num == 0:\n            return 0\n        \n        # Calculate f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)\n        sum_divisions = helper(num // 2) + helper(num // 3) + helper(num // 4) + helper(num // 5)\n        \n        # Return max of sum_divisions and n itself\n        result = max(sum_divisions, num)\n        memo[num] = result\n        return result\n    \n    return helper(n)"}
