{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum product subarray of the given array.\nassert max_subarray_product([1, -2, -3, 0, 7, -8, -2]) == 112\n\"\"\"\ndef max_subarray_product(nums):\n    \"\"\"Find the maximum product of contiguous subarray.\"\"\"\n    if not nums:\n        return 0\n    \n    max_prod = min_prod = result = nums[0]\n    \n    for i in range(1, len(nums)):\n        if nums[i] < 0:\n            max_prod, min_prod = min_prod, max_prod\n        \n        max_prod = max(nums[i], max_prod * nums[i])\n        min_prod = min(nums[i], min_prod * nums[i])\n        \n        result = max(result, max_prod)\n    \n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/468", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum product formed by multiplying numbers of an increasing subsequence of that array.\nassert max_product([3, 100, 4, 5, 150, 6]) == 3000\n\"\"\"\ndef max_product(arr):\n    \"\"\"Find maximum product of an increasing subsequence.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    # dp[i] stores the maximum product ending at index i\n    dp = arr[:]\n    \n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] * arr[i])\n    \n    return max(dp)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/468", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum product formed by multiplying numbers of an increasing subsequence of that array.\nassert max_product([3, 100, 4, 5, 150, 6]) == 3000\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef max_product(arr):\n    \"\"\"Find the maximum product of an increasing subsequence.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    dp = arr[:]\n    \n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] * arr[i])\n    \n    return max(dp)\n```"}
