{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the tuple intersection of elements in the given tuple list irrespective of their order.\nassert tuple_intersection([(3, 4), (5, 6), (9, 10), (4, 5)] , [(5, 4), (3, 4), (6, 5), (9, 11)]) == {(4, 5), (3, 4), (5, 6)}\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef tuple_intersection(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"Find intersection of tuples treating (a,b) and (b,a) as equivalent.\"\"\"\n    set1 = {tuple(sorted(t)) for t in list1}\n    set2 = {tuple(sorted(t)) for t in list2}\n    intersection = set1 & set2\n    \n    result = set()\n    for normalized_tuple in intersection:\n        for original_tuple in list1:\n            if tuple(sorted(original_tuple)) == normalized_tuple:\n                result.add(original_tuple)\n                break\n    \n    return result\n```"}
