{"task_id": "Mbpp/598", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to check whether the given number is armstrong or not.\nassert armstrong_number(153)==True\n\"\"\"\ndef armstrong_number(number):\n    \"\"\"Check if a number is an Armstrong number.\"\"\"\n    str_num = str(number)\n    num_digits = len(str_num)\n    digit_sum = sum(int(digit) ** num_digits for digit in str_num)\n    return digit_sum == number"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/599", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find sum and average of first n natural numbers.\nassert sum_average(10)==(55, 5.5)\n\"\"\"\ndef sum_average(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculate sum and average of first n natural numbers.\"\"\"\n    total = n * (n + 1) // 2\n    average = total / n\n    return (total, average)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find kth element from the given two sorted arrays.\nassert find_kth([2, 3, 6, 7, 9], [1, 4, 8, 10], 5) == 6\n\"\"\"\ndef find_kth(arr1, arr2, k):\n    \"\"\"Find the kth element from two sorted arrays. Uses merge-like approach to find element at position k-1.\"\"\"\n    i, j = 0, 0\n    count = 0\n    \n    while i < len(arr1) and j < len(arr2):\n        if arr1[i] <= arr2[j]:\n            if count == k - 1:\n                return arr1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            if count == k - 1:\n                return arr2[j]\n            j += 1\n        count += 1\n    \n    while i < len(arr1):\n        if count == k - 1:\n            return arr1[i]\n        i += 1\n        count += 1\n    \n    while j < len(arr2):\n        if count == k - 1:\n            return arr2[j]\n        j += 1\n        count += 1"}
