{"task_id": "Mbpp/605", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to check if the given integer is a prime number.\nassert prime_num(13)==True\n\"\"\"\ndef prime_num(n):\n    \"\"\"Check if given integer is a prime number.\"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return False\n    for i in range(2, int(n ** 0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to get all lucid numbers smaller than or equal to a given integer.\nassert get_ludic(10) == [1, 2, 3, 5, 7]\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef get_ludic(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns all ludic numbers up to and including n.\"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return []\n    \n    # Start with all numbers from 1 to n\n    numbers = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic = []\n    \n    while numbers:\n        # Take the first number as ludic\n        first = numbers[0]\n        ludic.append(first)\n        \n        # If first is 1, just remove it and continue\n        if first == 1:\n            numbers = numbers[1:]\n            continue\n            \n        # Remove every first-th number starting from the first occurrence\n        new_numbers = []\n        for i, num in enumerate(numbers):\n            if (i + 1) % first != 0:\n                new_numbers.append(num)\n        numbers = new_numbers\n    \n    return ludic\n```"}
