{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find nth bell number.\nassert bell_Number(2) == 2\n\"\"\"\ndef bell_Number(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the nth Bell number using dynamic programming with triangle method.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    bell = [[0 for i in range(n+1)] for j in range(n+1)]\n    bell[0][0] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(1, n+1):\n        bell[i][0] = bell[i-1][i-1]\n        for j in range(1, i+1):\n            bell[i][j] = bell[i-1][j-1] + bell[i][j-1]\n    \n    return bell[n][0]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find nth bell number.\nassert bell_Number(2) == 2\n\"\"\"\ndef bell_Number(n):\n    # Bell numbers using Bell triangle approach\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    bell = [[0 for i in range(n+1)] for j in range(n+1)]\n    bell[0][0] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(1, n+1):\n        bell[i][0] = bell[i-1][i-1]\n        for j in range(1, i+1):\n            bell[i][j] = bell[i-1][j-1] + bell[i][j-1]\n    \n    return bell[n][0]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/612", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function which takes a list of lists, where each sublist has two elements, and returns a list of two lists where the first list has the first element of each sublist and the second one has the second.\nassert merge([['x', 'y'], ['a', 'b'], ['m', 'n']]) == [['x', 'a', 'm'], ['y', 'b', 'n']]\n\"\"\"\ndef merge(pairs):\n    \"\"\"Splits a list of pairs into two separate lists by position.\"\"\"\n    if not pairs:\n        return [[], []]\n    first_elements = [pair[0] for pair in pairs]\n    second_elements = [pair[1] for pair in pairs]\n    return [first_elements, second_elements]"}
