{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the size of the largest subset of a list of numbers so that every pair is divisible.\nassert largest_subset([ 1, 3, 6, 13, 17, 18 ]) == 4\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef largest_subset(nums):\n    \"\"\"Find the size of the largest subset where every pair is divisible.\"\"\"\n    if not nums:\n        return 0\n    \n    nums.sort()\n    n = len(nums)\n    dp = [1] * n\n    \n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if nums[i] % nums[j] == 0:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n    \n    return max(dp)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the median of two sorted lists of same size.\nassert get_median([1, 12, 15, 26, 38], [2, 13, 17, 30, 45], 5) == 16.0\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef get_median(list1, list2, n):\n    \"\"\"Find median of two sorted lists of same size.\"\"\"\n    merged = []\n    i = j = 0\n    \n    while i < n and j < n:\n        if list1[i] <= list2[j]:\n            merged.append(list1[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            merged.append(list2[j])\n            j += 1\n    \n    while i < n:\n        merged.append(list1[i])\n        i += 1\n    \n    while j < n:\n        merged.append(list2[j])\n        j += 1\n    \n    return (merged[n - 1] + merged[n]) / 2.0\n```"}
